# Line endings.
#
# The shell scripts under app/src/main/assets are executed on the device by
# mksh. A CRLF line ending is not whitespace to mksh: the \r becomes part of the
# last token on the line, so `foo() {` parses as a syntax error and every
# variable assignment picks up a trailing CR. The app normalises CRLF when it
# extracts a script (FileWrite.parseText), but that is a safety net, not a
# licence to store them wrong - a CRLF script is also broken for anyone reading
# or running it straight out of the tree.
#
# Force LF for every script type that ends up on the device.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.prop text eol=lf
*.rc text eol=lf
